OpenRLHF v0.11.2 (17fd4a7) patches for the PPO / GRPO comparison.

1. LoRA weight sync to vLLM (openrlhf/trainer/ray/ppo_actor.py).
   Upstream broadcast_to_vllm sends the PEFT parameter names
   (base_model.model...base_layer.weight, lora_A, lora_B), which vLLM
   rejects ("no module or parameter named 'base_model'"), so any LoRA run
   with vLLM rollouts fails at the first weight sync. Still unfixed on
   upstream main (dc2a7ad, 2026-09-17). This sends W + scale * B @ A under
   the base names and skips the LoRA params.
   Checked: tiny GRPO at lr 2e-3 -- step-2 kl (policy vs v3) 0.054 while
   vllm_kl (vLLM vs policy) 8.7e-5, the same as before any update.

2. --train.critic_own_gpu (openrlhf/cli/train_ppo_ray.py).
   With --train.colocate_all the critic always shares the policy's GPU;
   with LoRA, DeepSpeed's sleep leaves each model's frozen 16 GB base on
   the GPU, so policy + critic + vLLM (~53 GB) don't fit one 46 GB L40S.
   The flag creates the critic outside the colocated placement group, so
   Ray puts it on a free GPU (here: a second node).
   Checked: tiny PPO on 2 GPUs (peaks 43.8 / 20.7 GB); at lr 2e-3 the
   KL penalty works (step-2 kl 0.034, return below reward).

Apply in an OpenRLHF v0.11.2 checkout:  git apply openrlhf_patches.patch
(or mount the patched files over the installed copies).

